  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run `vite build` or view the scene in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. In particular, I haven't confirmed that the camera auto-orbit and the shadow settings behave as I expect.\n\n- **Objects:** the scene has a ground plane and three instanced nodes, which is three draw calls for 10,000 objects. The nodes are 8,000 trunks (`instances.cylinder`), 8,000 canopies (`instances.cone`) and 2,000 rocks (`instances.sphere`, flattened and rotated).\n- **Placement:** a seeded LCG generator fixes the layout, so the forest is identical on every load. Objects are scattered in a disc of radius 62.\n- **Colour:** each trunk, canopy and rock gets its own HSL colour from the seed. The materials are white so the per-instance colour isn't multiplied by a base colour.\n- **Light and fog:** one directional light casts shadows, with a 4096 shadow map fitted over the forest. Fog is exponential (`effects.fog({ mode: \"exp\" })`). A neutral environment and a hemisphere light provide fill.\n- **Camera:** `camera.orbit` starts high and wide enough to show the whole forest. `interactions.orbit({ autoRotate: 0.08 })` is meant to turn it slowly around the centre.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set in the first `app.onFrame` callback. I didn't check whether that callback fires after the first frame is drawn or just before it.\n\n",
